From: shota <monyuonyu@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 21:58:49 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] Gears and belts keep the timing they were given first
 (phase)

The constant of a gear constraint was taken from the wheels as they were
at each solve, with angles measured within one turn: a wheel that had
moved kept its new timing, and a turn measured from the other side
shifted a cam by half a turn without a word. With a phase given, the
constant is the phase shifted by whole turns of either wheel to be the
nearest to the wheels' relation now (GearPhase.h); the constant of the
last solve can be read back (ASMTGearJoint::solvedConstant).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
